Guard ScalarEvolution cross-PHI recursion (SIGBUS/stack overflow in trustc)

Trust carries exactly one local change to LLVM. Building the compiler crashed
trustc with SIGBUS inside LLVM ScalarEvolution ("cycle encountered after 4
frames with period 15" through createAddRecFromPHI / createSimpleAffineAddRec /
createSCEV): createSimpleAffineAddRec evaluates the start/accum operands via
getSCEV BEFORE any placeholder is inserted into ValueExprMap, so a chain of
header PHIs whose operands reach back to the first PHI recurses unboundedly --
the general path's symbolic-name cycle breaker is never reached, because the
simple path runs first on every re-entry.

Fix: a PendingAddRecPHIs set (mirroring the existing PendingPhiRanges idiom)
guards createAddRecFromPHI. Re-entry for an in-progress PHI returns nullptr, so
that occurrence is modelled as a plain SCEVUnknown (a sound over-approximation)
and the outer construction completes and memoizes the precise AddRec. The set
is transient and scope-exit-erased; no invalidation plumbing is needed.

Validated by a full stage-2 build on default stacks with zero SIGBUS; the crash
was previously reproducible, and RUST_MIN_STACK=128M only outran it, which
confirmed unbounded recursion rather than a deep-but-finite stack.

Applies to the LLVM 22.1.x line (the tree Trust develops against is 22.1.2).
Upstream LLVM releases -- including distribution packages such as Homebrew's
llvm@22 -- carry the unguarded code, so an external LLVM must be patched and
rebuilt before it can host a Trust build. See patches/README.md.

Origin: Trust commit 1d1d11bed9fa32dfa20e45592dd748b0fef64e4d.

diff --git a/llvm/include/llvm/Analysis/ScalarEvolution.h b/llvm/include/llvm/Analysis/ScalarEvolution.h
index dcd11daf9e..cd0d55485e 100644
--- a/llvm/include/llvm/Analysis/ScalarEvolution.h
+++ b/llvm/include/llvm/Analysis/ScalarEvolution.h
@@ -1532,6 +1532,16 @@ private:
   // Mark SCEVUnknown Phis currently being processed by isImpliedViaMerge.
   SmallPtrSet<const PHINode *, 6> PendingMerges;
 
+  /// Set of Phis whose AddRec construction is in progress. Guards
+  /// createAddRecFromPHI against cross-PHI recursion cycles: the simple
+  /// affine path (createSimpleAffineAddRec) evaluates the start/accum
+  /// operands BEFORE any symbolic placeholder is inserted into
+  /// ValueExprMap, so a chain of header PHIs whose operands reach back to
+  /// the first PHI recurses without ever hitting the general path's
+  /// symbolic-name cycle breaker (observed as unbounded
+  /// createSCEV -> createAddRecFromPHI recursion; stack overflow).
+  SmallPtrSet<const PHINode *, 6> PendingAddRecPHIs;
+
   /// Set to true by isLoopBackedgeGuardedByCond when we're walking the set of
   /// conditions dominating the backedge of a loop.
   bool WalkingBEDominatingConds = false;
diff --git a/llvm/lib/Analysis/ScalarEvolution.cpp b/llvm/lib/Analysis/ScalarEvolution.cpp
index e19de5f46f..7c1fa27ab4 100644
--- a/llvm/lib/Analysis/ScalarEvolution.cpp
+++ b/llvm/lib/Analysis/ScalarEvolution.cpp
@@ -5807,6 +5807,17 @@ const SCEV *ScalarEvolution::createAddRecFromPHI(PHINode *PN) {
   if (!L || L->getHeader() != PN->getParent())
     return nullptr;
 
+  // Make sure we do not run over cycled PHIs (mirrors PendingPhiRanges):
+  // re-entering for a PHI already under construction means a cross-PHI
+  // operand cycle reached back here through createSimpleAffineAddRec's
+  // pre-placeholder getSCEV calls. Returning nullptr lets the caller model
+  // this occurrence as a plain SCEVUnknown — a sound over-approximation —
+  // and the outer in-progress construction completes and memoizes the
+  // precise AddRec.
+  if (!PendingAddRecPHIs.insert(PN).second)
+    return nullptr;
+  auto ClearPending = make_scope_exit([&]() { PendingAddRecPHIs.erase(PN); });
+
   // The loop may have multiple entrances or multiple exits; we can analyze
   // this phi as an addrec if it has a unique entry value and a unique
   // backedge value.
